  "id": "s03-l03",
  "unit": "s03-vowel-signs",
  "title": "Vowel signs 3: ে ৈ",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**ে and ৈ go on the left**, just like ি. Read the consonant first, then the sign's vowel: **কে** is `ke`, not *ek*. দেশ = দ + ে + শ = `desh`; কেমন = `kemon`; মেয়ে = `meye`.\n\n**ে has two pronunciations**: `e` as in *bed* (দেশ) or an open sound like the *a* in *cat* in some words (দেখা in আবার দেখা হবে). Transliteration writes both as `e`, so let the audio guide you.\n\n**ৈ** is ে with a little flick on top and says `oi` (*boy*): তৈরি (`toiri`, ready), পহেলা বৈশাখ (`pohela boishakh`, Bengali New Year).\n\nWarning for next lesson: if you see ে on the left **and** া on the right of the same letter, that's one sign, ো (`o`).",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "k-e",
      "bn": "কে",
      "tr": "ke",
      "en": "ে (e-kar): adds 'e' as in 'bed' or 'ay' as in 'say'",
      "notes": "Bare sign: ে (U+09C7), name e-kar (এ-কার). Drawn to the LEFT of the consonant. কে also means 'who?'. Sometimes said æ (দেখা dækha)."
    },
    {
      "id": "k-oi",
      "bn": "কৈ",
      "tr": "koi",
      "en": "ৈ (oi-kar): adds 'oi' as in 'boy'",
      "notes": "Bare sign: ৈ (U+09C8), name oi-kar (ঐ-কার). ে with an extra flick on top; also drawn to the left."
    },
    {
      "id": "toiri",
      "bn": "তৈরি",
      "tr": "toiri",
      "en": "made / ready",
      "notes": "তৈরি করা = to make; আমি তৈরি = I'm ready. তৈরী is an older, non-standard spelling (Bangla Academy: তৈরি)."
    }
  ],
